"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI visited this cafe wanting to spend some leisurely time after a while.  \nIt was a place where I previously enjoyed delicious bread, so I revisited with fond memories.  \n\nParking around here is somewhat tricky, as the alleys are narrow and spaces seem limited.  \nIf you circle around a few times, you might get lucky and find an open spot.  \n\nThere is a dedicated space for the resident cat, and they say if you're lucky, the cat comes out to greet you.  \nUnfortunately, we only got to see the cat fast asleep.  \nStill, just watching it sleep peacefully melted my heart.  \n\nWe ordered the bread I had enjoyed previously along with a new dessert we wanted to try and coffee, then settled into a corner seat.  \nPlanning to take our time and do various things leisurely, we deliberately tucked ourselves away in the corner.  \nThanks to that, we could chat comfortably without feeling self-conscious and stay for a long while.  \n\nFortunately, we went a bit early, so there weren't many guests.  \nThe cafe interior was quiet with lovely sunlight streaming in, making it a great atmosphere to linger.  \n\nWith delicious bread and solid coffee, there were quite a few delivery orders as well.  \nSeeing the staff constantly packaging takeout orders, it seemed quietly popular in the neighborhood.  \n\nThanks to all that, we had a wonderful and relaxing time.  \nIt's a place I'd love to drop by again whenever I'm in the neighborhood.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"